OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31302
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FResearchers from the British
OL,7,FGeological Survey (BGS) have found
OL,8,Fthat groundwater levels across the
OL,9,Fcountry remain robust, and in some
OL,10,Fcases higher than normal, despite two-
OL,11,Fthirds of England and Wales currently
OL,12,Fin drought.
OL,14,FThe string of heatwaves and lack of
OL,15,Frainfall this summer has resulted in
OL,16,Frapidly declining reservoir stocks and
OL,17,Fgrowing surface water shortages,
OL,18,Fleading to hosepipe bans and severe
OL,19,Fimpacts on agriculture, wildlife and
OL,20,Finfrastructure.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31303
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FWhile reservoir storage for England
OL,7,Fstood at 85% at the end of June, the
OL,8,FEnvironment Agency revealed on Friday
OL,9,Fthat it now stands at 66%, nearly 14
OL,10,Fpercentage points below the long-term
OL,11,Faverage for the time of year.
OL,13,FYet the country's groundwater mostly
OL,14,Fremains at normal or even above normal
OL,15,Flevels after healthy replenishment
OL,16,Fduring this year's wet winter months,
OL,17,Fthe BGS scientists found.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31304
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FBGS head of environmental modelling,
OL,7,FChristopher Jackson, said: "There's
OL,8,Ffar more storage in our groundwater
OL,9,Fsystems than there is in our surface
OL,10,Fwater reservoirs or our rivers, so
OL,11,Fit's a huge store of water.
OL,13,F"So it is remarkable in that context `
OL,14,Fthat even though you can get this
OL,15,Fexceptional heat and surface water
OL,16,Fdrought, groundwater is doing OK."
OL,18,FThe team analysed aquifer levels from
OL,19,Fdozens of borehole monitoring sites
OL,20,Faround the UK at the end of July.
OL,26,@oD@\OUuD@AOUxD@bO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31305
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FThey then compared them to historical
OL,7,Frecords that span at least several
OL,8,Fdecades, and even date back 191 years
OL,9,Ffor the Chilgrove House site in West
OL,10,FSussex.
OL,12,FOut of 35 groundwater sites analysed,
OL,13,F15 reported "normal" or "above normal
OL,14,Flevels" compared with historical
OL,15,Fmeasurements for this time of year,
OL,16,Fmaking up 43%.
OL,26,@uD@MOUuD@TO]uD@YOUvD@GO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31306
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FOnly eight sites, or 23%, were showing
OL,7,F"notably below normal levels" and a
OL,8,Fhandful of sites are close to the
OL,9,Flowest end of the historical average,
OL,10,Fbut none show record lows, the team
OL,11,Ffound.
OL,13,FThe scientists added that every summer
OL,14,Fgroundwater levels naturally fall and
OL,15,Fso it is normal to see notably low
OL,16,Flevels in some places.
OL,26,@oD@AOUoD@]O]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31307
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FThe data shows North Wales, the
OL,7,FMidlands, East Anglia, Kent, Devon and
OL,8,FCornwall, all of which are currently
OL,9,Fin drought, have particularly healthy
OL,10,Faquifers in comparison to their
OL,11,Fsurface water resources.
OL,13,FHead of BGS Groundwater, Alan
OL,14,FMacDonald, said: "Scientists have long
OL,15,Fknown that groundwater is a naturally
OL,16,Fresilient water source.
OL,26,@vD@ROU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31308
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,F"While surface water resources often
OL,7,Fgrab the headlines as they are such a
OL,8,Fvisual reference point, groundwater is
OL,9,Foften overlooked as one of the
OL,10,Fcountry's primary water sources.
OL,12,F"The extreme weather conditions this
OL,13,Fsummer have really highlighted how
OL,14,Frobust these reserves are and indicate
OL,15,Fthat they could play a much bigger
OL,16,Frole in mitigating the impacts of
OL,17,Fclimate change in future."
OL,26,@nD@AOUtD@AOUyD@ZO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31309
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FThe team said the data suggests there
OL,7,Fmay be an opportunity to revisit
OL,8,Fcurrent thresholds for pumping
OL,9,Fgroundwater into the environment so
OL,10,Fthat more supplies are made available
OL,11,Fduring future periods of drought.
OL,13,FA handful of so-called "groundwater
OL,14,Faugmentation schemes" are already
OL,15,Funderway, including an Environment
OL,16,FAgency initiative to pump groundwater
OL,17,Finto the River Severn in periods of
OL,18,Fdry weather.
OL,26,@uD@XOUvD@UO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
