PN,31310
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FSubscribe for free to our weekly
OL,7,Fnewsletter for exclusive and original
OL,8,Fcoverage from ITV News. Direct to your
OL,9,Finbox every Friday morning.
OL,11,FAt full capacity, this scheme can
OL,12,Frelease up to 240 million litres of
OL,13,Fwater a day to help maintain river
OL,14,Flevels, protecting water suppliers and
OL,15,Fwildlife habitats in periods of hot
OL,16,Fdry weather before they are
OL,17,Freplenished during wetter months.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31311
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FMore widely, concerns remain over
OL,7,Fabstraction's impact on the
OL,8,Fenvironment, such as drying up rare
OL,9,Fchalk streams and other habitats.
OL,11,FWhile more research into the issue is
OL,12,Frequired, Mr Jackson said: "There are
OL,13,Fpossibilities to more cleverly think
OL,14,Fabout where you pump groundwater to
OL,15,Fminimise the impacts on summer low
OL,16,Fflows, whilst also maintaining public
OL,17,Fwater supply."
OL,26,@tD@\OUyD@NO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31312
SC,0012
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,FThe scientists acknowledged years with
OL,7,Fdrier winters could leave groundwater
OL,8,Flevels more vulnerable to dry summers
OL,9,Fas weather patterns become more
OL,10,Fvolatile with climate change.
OL,12,F"Summers are going to get drier.
OL,13,FWinters are probably going to get
OL,14,Fwetter," Mr Jackson said. "But what
OL,15,Fthat means, how that translates into
OL,16,Fgroundwater resources and water
OL,17,Fresources, is a bit more uncertain.
OL,26,@tD@AOUvD@HO]vD@[OU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G12/13
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,314,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31313
SC,0013
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F313A1786906081
OL,3,CUK groundwater levels in 'remarkable'
OL,4,Chealth despite drought, scientists find
OL,6,F"We are going to see more severe
OL,7,Fdroughts in the future and so we're
OL,8,Fgoing to have to build more resilience
OL,9,Finto our public water supply.
OL,11,F"Groundwater systems are a little bit
OL,12,Fmore resilient to drought, but there
OL,13,Fis going to have to be more clever
OL,14,Fways of managing through these
OL,15,Fdroughts, and the water industry is
OL,16,Faware of that and is working towards
OL,17,Fhow we adapt."
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@AOUyD@NO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G13/13
